      {
        "t": "key",
        "html": "<b>ten</b>, <b>tain</b>, <b>tin</b> = <b>hold</b>. <b>pend</b>, <b>pens</b> = <b>hang, weigh, pay</b>. <b>fer</b> = <b>carry, bear</b>. <b>fund</b>, <b>fus</b> = <b>pour</b>."
      },
      {
        "t": "p",
        "html": "Long ago, money was weighed out on scales, so <i>pend</i> (weigh) also came to mean “pay”: <i>expensive</i> things need much money weighed out. And a <b>pensive</b> person is weighing thoughts."
      },
      {
        "t": "h",
        "text": "The parts and their words"
      },
