      {
        "t": "h",
        "text": "Words taken apart"
      },
      {
        "t": "table",
        "head": [
          "Word and meaning",
          "Parts, and what they say"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "<b>tenacious</b><br>holding firmly to something; persistent",
            "<b>ten</b> <i>hold</i> + -acious<br>→ “holding fast”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>tenet</b><br>a principle held as true by a group",
            "<b>ten</b> <i>hold</i> + -et<br>→ “a thing held (true)”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>untenable</b><br>not able to be defended",
            "un- <i>not</i> + <b>ten</b> <i>hold</i> + -able <i>able to be</i><br>→ “not able to be held”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>abstain</b><br>to choose not to do or have something",
            "abs- <i>away</i> + <b>tain</b> <i>hold</i><br>→ “hold away from”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>sustain</b><br>to keep going; to support",
            "sus- <i>from under</i> + <b>tain</b> <i>hold</i><br>→ “hold up from under”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>propensity</b><br>a natural tendency to behave a certain way",
            "pro- <i>forward</i> + <b>pens</b> <i>hang</i> + -ity<br>→ “a hanging forward (a leaning)”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>pensive</b><br>deeply thoughtful, often sadly",
            "<b>pens</b> <i>weigh</i> + -ive<br>→ “weighing (thoughts)”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>infer</b><br>to reach a conclusion from evidence or hints",
            "in- <i>in</i> + <b>fer</b> <i>carry</i><br>→ “carry in (to a conclusion)”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>profuse</b><br>plentiful; pouring out",
            "pro- <i>forth</i> + <b>fus</b> <i>pour</i> + -e<br>→ “poured forth”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>diffuse</b><br>to spread out",
            "dif- <i>apart</i> + <b>fus</b> <i>pour</i> + -e<br>→ “poured apart”"
          ]
        ],
        "cap": "Each word, what it means now, and its parts."
      },
      {
        "t": "ex",
        "title": "Use the parts",
        "q": "Grandma’s new couch was <b>expensive</b>. What does the root tell you about the word?",
        "steps": [
          "Take it apart: <b>ex-</b> (out) + <b>pens</b> (weigh, pay) + <b>-ive</b> (tending to).",
          "Long ago, coins were weighed out on scales to pay for things.",
          "An expensive thing needs a lot of money weighed out."
        ],
        "a": "Costing a lot of money."
      },
